{"content":"h15.\n\nHere are the distinct enforcement sites for memo visibility, grouped by the surface area they protect:\n\n1. **ListMemos (memo listing query filter)** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go` (lines 218–227)\n   Restricts `VisibilityList`/adds a filter so unauthenticated users see only PUBLIC and non-owners see only PUBLIC+PROTECTED.\n\n2. **GetMemo / UpdateMemo (`checkMemoReadAccess` helper)** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go` (lines 39–68)\n   Point-read guard: blocks unauthenticated users from non-PUBLIC memos, blocks non-owners from PRIVATE memos. Called for `GetMemo` (line 356) and `UpdateMemo` (line 367).\n\n3. **CreateMemoComment / ListMemoComments** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go`\n   Direct PRIVATE-visibility check before allowing comment creation (line 41), plus `checkMemoReadAccess` (line 148) and a visibility filter on comment listing (lines 157–161).\n\n4. **ListMemoRelations (relation listing query filter)** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_relation_service.go` (lines 108–112)\n   Applies a `memoFilter` string (`visibility == \"PUBLIC\"` or PUBLIC+PROTECTED) when listing related memos.\n\n5. **Batch relation conversion in memo converter** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go` (lines 182–187)\n   Same visibility filter applied during `batchConvertMemoRelations` so related-memo snippets are visibility-scoped.\n\n6. **ListMemoReactions / UpsertMemoReaction** — `server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go` (lines 29–41, 82–85)\n   Checks the parent memo's visibility before listing or upserting reactions.\n\n7. **ListMemoAttachments** — `server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go` (lines 213–225)\n   Checks memo visibility before returning the memo's attachments.\n\n8. **GetAttachment (`checkAttachmentAccess`)** — `server/router/api/v1/attachment_service.go` (lines 255–258, 422–455)\n   For linked attachments, enforces memo visibility: PUBLIC → open, PRIVATE → owner-only.\n\n9. **User stats** — `server/router/api/v1/user_service_stats.go` (lines 84, 90, 218, 220)\n   `ListAllUserStats` and `GetUserStats` restrict the memo query via `VisibilityList`.\n\n10. **SSE event delivery filtering** — `server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go` (lines 134–144)\n    `canReceive` on each SSE client filters events by visibility: PRIVATE events only delivered to the creator or admin.\n\n11. **In-app notifications** — `server/router/api/v1/user_service_notifications.go` (lines 302–316, 337, 342, 370, 385)\n    `canViewerAccessMemo` suppresses notification details when the receiver lacks visibility to the memo.\n\n12. **Email notifications** — `server/notification/email.go` (lines 155, 187, 306–320)\n    Parallel `canViewerAccessMemo` suppresses email content for memos the recipient can't see.\n\n13. **Sitemap** — `server/router/frontend/frontend.go` (line 150)\n    Only PUBLIC memos included in the sitemap XML.\n\n14. **RSS feeds** — `server/router/rss/rss.go` (lines 90, 141)\n    Both global and per-user RSS feeds restrict to PUBLIC-only memos.","iteration":9,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
